nina: Meridian fintech wants an end-to-end example: WebSocket SSE, signed envelopes from their HSM, and deterministic tool/function call schema. Also asked about cost implications.

omar: We have JS/Go SDKs supporting chunked SSE. Handshake pattern: client connects, sends short-lived token, then sends signed envelope header `x-signed-envelope`.

sec-team: Supported algos: ECDSA-P256 and RSA-PSS. For Private deployments we can integrate customer HSM (PKCS#11). Hosted BYOK supports importing keys into tenant HSMs; no private key export.

omar: Minimal JS snippet:```js
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://edge.redwood.ai/v1/stream');
ws.onopen = () => {
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({type:'auth',token:'SHORT'}));
  // attach signed envelope as header on initial request
};
```

nina: For structured tool calls, suggest fields: `schema_version`, `idempotency_key`, `signed_schema_hash`. Sample body: `{"action":"pay","amount":250.0,"currency":"USD","idempotency_key":"uuid"}`. Recommend idempotency ACKs to avoid double-exec on reconnect.

infra: Pricing: token billing unchanged; Dedicated with reserved capacity has per-connection-minute for long-lived sockets. Send them a short matrix.

presales-bot: Action created: meridian-edge-poc (assignees: nina, omar) due in 48h :white_check_mark:

nina: I'll combine these into an email and include SDK versions (JS >=0.11, Go >=0.9.4) and the legal blurb for BYOK.
